# Spirit Wolf

## Lore

It looks like an ordinary large grey wolf and it is a creature of magic with low
human intelligence and incredible cunning. It mostly lives as a wolf, but finds
humans, D-Bees and other intelligent creatures irresistibly interesting, and
watches their affairs from a distance.

From time to time it joins adventurers, heroes or brigands for the fun of it, or
adopts a village as its unofficial protector. Then one day it announces it is
leaving, or simply disappears - the Great Wolf hates being confined, and finds
responsibility, even to friends, too restricting.

It never forgets a friend or an enemy, and is always glad to meet old friends
again.

## Alignment

Any, but the vast majority are anarchist (40%), unprincipled (30%), aberrant
(10%) or miscreant (10%).

## GM Notes

**It understands human law perfectly well and does not think it applies to
it.** That is a different problem from the Leshii and the Polevoi, who do not
understand it at all, and it makes the Spirit Wolf the most socially capable of
the six - most are natural, cunning con-artists who can talk candy out of the
mouth of babes.

**It is at its most dangerous when bored.** The book recommends two to twelve
days in civilization before the obstinacy and the sarcasm start.

It is the fastest thing in the book: **82 mph, held for 72 hours**. Electrical
attacks do double damage to it, and silver S.D.C. weapons inflict M.D.
', 'published', 'data-script'
